{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Sorry we're late. The bus died on Maple and the next one took forever.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Uh, hang on. It just kicked me out again. Password... okay. There.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CAREGIVER): We were aiming for ten. Wasn't even traffic, it was the bus.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right, right. Sorry, what was that? I'm half in this chart.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Just that we got held up. He's been sitting fine, watching the fish tank out there.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Okay. So what brings him in?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): High INR.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): High INR. Say that again? This fan is right on the mic.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): INR.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Anticoagulation clinic called yesterday. Said the warfarin number was up and to come on in.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me open the lab. Umm. INR is three point two... no, that's last month. Today's is three point nine.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): Bad?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): It's above range. For the atrial fibrillation we want it between two and three. What dose of warfarin is he actually on?",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Two and a half milligrams... no, sorry, that's old. It's five. Five milligrams every night for the afib.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Five milligrams at night. Coumadin, warfarin, same drug. Still for the afib, yeah?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): Yes.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Years now. The heart doctor started it.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any bleeding? Nose, gums, black stools, urine?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Bruises? Sorry, say it again, any bruises?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): None.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (CAREGIVER): He did get put on an antibiotic. Urgent care, for a urine infection.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Err, which antibiotic? I can't read their note, the scan came out sideways.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (CAREGIVER): She said amoxicillin. No, wait, I looked at the bottle. It's ciproflaxacin. Five hundred, twice a day.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ciprofloxacin, five hundred twice a day. How many days has he had it?",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (CAREGIVER): A week... no. Three days. He's had three days of it for the urine infection.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): Three.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Three days. And somebody wrote something about greens. What happened with the spinach?",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Big spinach salad every lunch, usually. Hasn't eaten it since the cipro. Says it tastes awful now.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Did you say every day? Repeat that for me.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Every day, till this week. Nothing green, really.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Alright. Less vitamin K plus the cipro, that's why the INR climbed. I'm calling it a high INR from those two things, not a new bleed.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Plan is skip the warfarin tonight. Starting tomorrow, four milligrams every night. Not five.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): Four.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (CAREGIVER): And the antibiotic, does he finish it?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Yes, finish the cipro. We'll recheck the INR in a week, front desk will book it. Hold off on the big salads till that next number, then keep the greens the same amount each day. Any bleeding, you call."
 ],
